        "original_id": "dc5f89b4-fd96-5315-a536-4eca6a13206d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Dey, Alfred Gough, Miles Millar, Roger Yuan, Jackie Chan, Chow Yun-fat\n- Works: Shanghai Noon, Showtime, Failure to Launch, Marmaduke, Bulletproof Monk, Batman Begins, Skyfall\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, producer, actor\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Dey was born on April 14, 1965, and he is an American film director, screenwriter, and producer.\n- Shanghai Noon marked the directorial debut of Tom Dey.\n- Alfred Gough and Miles Millar wrote Shanghai Noon.\n- Roger Yuan appeared in Shanghai Noon (2000) opposite Jackie Chan.\n- Roger Yuan appeared in Bulletproof Monk (2003) alongside Chow Yun-fat.\n- Roger Yuan played the technician in Batman Begins (2005).\n- Roger Yuan played Severine's bodyguard in Skyfall (2012).\n- Tom Dey's credits include Shanghai Noon, Showtime, Failure to Launch, and Marmaduke.",
